    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d294-a6">

                <pb facs="0491" n="419" xml:id="pg419"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Appendix to inclosure.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">General Sherman to
                        Mr. Lincoln.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tucson, Ariz.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1882-04-11"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 11,
                        1882</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I beg to acknowledge receipt, through
                    General McDowell’s headquarters, of a copy of the communication of March 1,
                    1882, from the honorable Secretary of State, transmitting a communication from
                    the Mexican minister, reporting depredations in Mexico by Indians from the San
                    Carlos Reservation, and to report that I have been in person to that
                    reservation, as also on the Mexican border; that since October, 1881, there have
                    been no Indians from the San Carlos Reservation in Mexico; that the Chiricahuas
                    who then escaped fled from a supposed personal danger, and are now in Mexico,
                    but that the Mexican military authorities were unwilling to permit our troops to
                    pursue and capture them, expressing their ability to take care of them, and that
                    since, up to the present moment, effectual measures have been taken by the
                    military authorities of the United States to prevent any similar
                    recurrences.</p>
                <p>So far as my knowledge goes there is perfect peace along the national border at
                    this time.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>W. T. SHERMAN,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                    >General.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
